<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Commonwealth cuts some mortgage rates.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Commonwealth cuts some mortgage rates.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Bank of Australia said it cut 0.4 point off its One Year Guaranteed housing loan interest rate for owner occupier and investment borrowers.</p>
<p>The owner occupied rate was reduced to 7.50 percent from 7.90 percent, while the investment rate fell to 8.10 percent from 8.50 percent. The bank also cut its establishment fee for the loan to A$300 from A$600.</p>
<p>The CBA said it was also waiving its A$600 establishment fee for the Economiser home loan for a limited time, and extending a special offer of waiving the fee on the Standard Variable Rate loan.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
